# SDD Specification: RBJ-115 Passkey login

## 1. Goal
Invited users accept an invite by entering name/phone, then authenticating with Microsoft Entra/passkey, then receiving a normal internal Workslip JWT. Backend enrollment must revalidate invite state at callback time, create Entra + SQL user atomically enough to avoid orphaned Entra users when SQL persistence fails, mark invite consumed only after SQL success, and return the same `AuthTokenResponse` shape as existing login/invite flows.

## 2. Non-goals
- Do not rewrite existing email-code login.
- Do not change existing `/api/auth/verify-invite/{token}` response shape unless kept for backwards compatibility.
- Do not add AI/OCR scope. Selvfølgelig ikke.
- Do not touch unrelated jobs/audit/history features.
- Do not add new UI routes beyond the existing `/invite/:token` flow unless OAuth callback handling proves a dedicated callback route is required.

## 3. Current System Findings
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Endpoints/AuthEndpoints.cs`: existing auth group exposes `/send-code`, `/verify-code/{code}`, `/verify-invite/{token}`, `/invite`, `/invites`, `/invite/{token}/open`.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Application/Auth/AuthContracts.cs`: `AuthTokenResponse`, `AuthUserInfo`, `VerifyInviteRequest`, and `CompleteInviteRequest` already exist. Add `EntraEnrollRequest` here.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Application/Invitations/InvitationService.cs`: `VerifyInviteAsync` currently creates Entra user, creates SQL user, marks invite consumed, then returns `AuthUserInfo`; no transaction and no Entra cleanup on SQL failure.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Application/Invitations/IInvitationService.cs`: only exposes `VerifyInviteAsync`; add `CompleteEnrollmentAsync` for new endpoint.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Application/Users/IUserEntraService.cs`: only has `CreateUserAsync`; add `DeleteUserAsync` for rollback cleanup.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Application/Users/UserEntraService.cs`: creates Entra user via Microsoft Graph and assigns app role. Add delete method using Graph user delete.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Infrastructure/Repositories/EfUserRepository.cs`: `CreateAsync` calls `SaveChangesAsync` immediately.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Infrastructure/Repositories/EfInviteRepository.cs`: `MarkConsumedAsync` calls `SaveChangesAsync` immediately.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Infrastructure/Schema/SqlDbContext.cs`: EF context owns SQL transaction API, but Application layer currently does not depend on Infrastructure. Add a small Application transaction abstraction rather than leaking `SqlDbContext` into Application.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Configuration/AuthenticationConfiguration.cs`: app already accepts both internal JWT and Entra JWT via combined bearer scheme; Entra tokens can hit API endpoints when `RequireAuthorization()` is applied.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Helpers/UserClaimsTransformation.cs`: unknown Entra user stays authenticated but no Workslip claims. Enrollment endpoint must not require `RequireUser`, only a valid Entra bearer token.
- `src/FE/src/features/auth/routes/InviteAccept.tsx`: current invite flow validates/open-marks invite, collects displayName/phone, calls `/api/auth/verify-invite/{token}`, stores internal token, and shows success.
- `src/FE/src/features/auth/api/inviteAccept.ts`: contains direct axios wrappers for invite accept/open.
- `src/FE/package.json`: no `oidc-react`, `@azure/msal-browser`, or OIDC client dependency exists. Linear description mentions `oidc-react`, but repo does not have it. Use minimal direct OAuth/OIDC helper unless dependency addition is explicitly approved.
- `src/FE/src/lib/axios.ts`: axios request interceptor attaches internal Workslip token from `AUTH_TOKEN_KEY`; enrollment call must pass Entra access token explicitly so it does not accidentally use an old internal token.

## 4. Architecture Decision
Backend: add `POST /api/auth/entra-enroll` and keep existing `/verify-invite/{token}` for compatibility. Enrollment accepts token/name/phone, requires a valid Entra bearer token, revalidates invite at execution time, starts an EF-backed transaction via an Application abstraction, creates/ensures Entra user, creates SQL user, marks invite consumed, commits, then returns `AuthUserInfo` mapped through existing `JwtHelper.GenerateToken` to `AuthTokenResponse`. If SQL/user/invite persistence fails after Entra creation, rollback transaction and call `DeleteUserAsync` to remove the Entra user.

Frontend: update `InviteAccept.tsx` into a two-phase flow. First collect/display persist name+phone+invite token in `sessionStorage`. Then start Microsoft OAuth authorization-code-with-PKCE flow using existing Azure/OAuth env vars. On return to `/invite`, exchange auth code for an Entra access token, call `/api/auth/entra-enroll` with explicit `Authorization: Bearer <entraAccessToken>`, store internal Workslip JWT, clean invite session keys and PKCE verifier, redirect to app/profile.

Reason: avoids sending PII in URL, preserves existing API shape, uses current combined auth scheme, and avoids Application depending directly on Infrastructure. The issue text says `oidc-react`; codebase says nope. Code wins. Fight me.

## 5. File-Level Change Plan
### Create
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Application/Common/IApplicationTransaction.cs`: transaction abstraction with `CommitAsync`, `RollbackAsync`, `DisposeAsync`.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Application/Common/IApplicationTransactionFactory.cs`: begins transactions from Application layer.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Infrastructure/Transactions/EfApplicationTransaction.cs`: wraps EF Core `IDbContextTransaction`.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Infrastructure/Transactions/EfApplicationTransactionFactory.cs`: uses `SqlDbContext.Database.BeginTransactionAsync`.
- `src/FE/src/features/auth/api/entraInviteEnrollment.ts`: local FE helper for OAuth PKCE, token exchange, sessionStorage keys, and `/api/auth/entra-enroll` call.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Tests/Invitations/InvitationEnrollmentTests.cs`: focused service-level tests with fakes, because no API test factory exists in current test project.

### Modify
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Application/Auth/AuthContracts.cs`:
  - Add `public sealed record EntraEnrollRequest(string Token, string DisplayName, string? Phone);`.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Application/Invitations/IInvitationService.cs`:
  - Add `Task<Result<AuthUserInfo>> CompleteEnrollmentAsync(EntraEnrollRequest request, CancellationToken cancellationToken);`.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Application/Invitations/InvitationService.cs`:
  - Inject `IApplicationTransactionFactory`.
  - Add `CompleteEnrollmentAsync` with revalidation, transaction, Entra cleanup on failure, org logging, and same `AuthUserInfo` output.
  - Preserve `VerifyInviteAsync` behavior or delegate to a shared internal method without changing public API response.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Application/Users/IUserEntraService.cs`:
  - Add `Task DeleteUserAsync(string entraUserId, CancellationToken ct);`.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Application/Users/UserEntraService.cs`:
  - Implement `DeleteUserAsync` with Graph delete and structured logging.
  - If Graph delete fails during rollback, log and rethrow only after preserving original SQL exception context where possible.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Infrastructure/DependencyInjection.cs`:
  - Register `IApplicationTransactionFactory` to `EfApplicationTransactionFactory`.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Endpoints/AuthEndpoints.cs`:
  - Add `POST /api/auth/entra-enroll` mapping to `IInvitationService.CompleteEnrollmentAsync` and `ResultExtensions.ToHttpResult(result, user => JwtHelper.GenerateToken(user, configuration))`.
  - Endpoint must require any authenticated Entra bearer token, not `RequireUser`.
- `src/FE/src/features/auth/api/inviteAccept.ts`:
  - Add or delegate `enrollInviteWithEntra(...)` wrapper using explicit bearer token.
- `src/FE/src/features/auth/routes/InviteAccept.tsx`:
  - Replace one-step submit with `collectingInfo -> authenticating -> enrolling -> success/error` states.
  - Persist displayName/phone/token to sessionStorage before Microsoft redirect.
  - On OAuth callback, restore session data, call enroll endpoint, store internal token, clean session keys, redirect/show success.
  - Keep existing invite invalid/expired/consumed messages.

### Do Not Touch
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Infrastructure/Schema/DatabaseSeeder.cs`: not needed.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Infrastructure/Schema/Audit*`: unrelated; original main worktree has audit edits, avoid cross-contamination.
- Generated Orval files under `src/FE/src/api/generated/**`: avoid manual generated edits; direct apiClient wrapper is sufficient.
- Existing login email-code route/components except import-safe shared helper usage.

## 6. API Contract
### Request
`POST /api/auth/entra-enroll`
Headers:
```json
{ "Authorization": "Bearer <valid Entra access token>" }
```
Body:
```json
{
  "token": "invite-token-guid-without-dashes",
  "displayName": "Jane Jensen",
  "phone": "+45 12 34 56 78"
}
```
`phone` may be null/omitted/empty.

### Response
Same as existing auth responses:
```json
{
  "token": "<internal Workslip JWT>",
  "tokenType": "Bearer",
  "expiresIn": 3600,
  "user": {
    "userId": "guid",
    "organizationId": "guid",
    "email": "invitee@example.com",
    "displayName": "Jane Jensen",
    "role": "User"
  }
}
```

### Compatibility
- Preserve `/api/auth/verify-invite/{token}` response shape.
- Preserve `AuthTokenResponse` shape exactly.
- Preserve existing conflict codes: `invite_consumed`, `invite_expired`, `user_already_exists`.
- `POST /api/auth/invite/{token}/open` remains open/anonymous.

## 7. Data/Type Contract
- `EntraEnrollRequest.Token`: required non-empty string; maps to existing `InviteTokenRow.Token`.
- `DisplayName`: required non-empty after trim; max should respect `Users.DisplayName` max 200.
- `Phone`: optional; trim before save; max should respect `Users.Phone` max 80.
- `UserDataRow` remains unchanged.
- `InviteTokenRow` remains unchanged.
- Frontend sessionStorage keys must be namespaced, e.g. `workslip.inviteEnrollment` and `workslip.invitePkce`.
- Entra token must never be stored under `AUTH_TOKEN_KEY`; only final Workslip JWT goes there.

## 8. Behavior Rules
- Given invite token missing, when user opens `/invite/:token`, show invalid invite state.
- Given invite valid, when user enters name/phone and continues, save invite enrollment data to sessionStorage before redirecting to Microsoft.
- Given Microsoft returns with `code`, when sessionStorage invite data exists, exchange code for Entra access token, call `/api/auth/entra-enroll`, save internal JWT, cleanup temporary session keys.
- Given invite expired/consumed during Microsoft redirect, backend returns conflict code and frontend shows existing Danish message.
- Given SQL user creation or invite consumption fails after Entra user creation, backend rolls back SQL transaction and calls `DeleteUserAsync` for created Entra user.
- Given Entra user already exists because `CreateUserAsync` found existing one, cleanup delete must be careful: if service cannot distinguish created-vs-existing, spec requires either extend result with `Created` flag or avoid deleting pre-existing users. Better approach: extend `CreateEntraUserResult` with `bool Created` and only delete when `Created == true`.
- Given unknown Entra user hits `/api/auth/entra-enroll`, endpoint still may execute because it only needs valid Entra authentication and invite token; it must not require Workslip claims.
- Given old internal token is present in sessionStorage, enrollment call must explicitly override Authorization with Entra token.

## 9. Test Plan
### Failing tests first
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Tests/Invitations/InvitationEnrollmentTests.cs::CompleteEnrollmentAsync_WhenSqlCreateFails_DeletesNewEntraUserAndDoesNotConsumeInvite`: fake repositories throw on SQL create, assert fake Entra delete called once, transaction rollback called, invite not consumed.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Tests/Invitations/InvitationEnrollmentTests.cs::CompleteEnrollmentAsync_WhenInviteExpired_ReturnsConflictAndDoesNotCreateEntraUser`: expired invite returns `invite_expired` and no Entra create/delete.
- `src/BE/WorkslipApi/Workslip.Tests/Invitations/InvitationEnrollmentTests.cs::CompleteEnrollmentAsync_WhenSuccess_CommitsMarksConsumedAndReturnsAuthUser`: success returns expected `AuthUserInfo`, commit called once.

### Regression tests
- `dotnet test Workslip.Tests/Workslip.Tests.csproj --no-restore --logger 'console;verbosity=minimal' -p:OutputPath=C:/Workslip/.tmp/test-out/$(date +%s)/`
- `dotnet build Workslip.Api.csproj --no-restore -v minimal -o /c/Workslip/.tmp/api-build-$(date +%s)`
- `cd /c/Workslip-worktrees/workslip-new-feature-20260612-154404/src/FE && npm exec tsc -- -b --pretty false`
- `cd /c/Workslip-worktrees/workslip-new-feature-20260612-154404/src/FE && npm run build -- --mode development`

### Manual/API verification
- Use Postman/curl with valid Entra bearer token:
  - `POST /api/auth/entra-enroll` with valid invite -> 200 `AuthTokenResponse`.
  - Repeat same invite -> 409 `invite_consumed`.
  - Expired invite -> 409 `invite_expired`.
- Browser flow: open invite link, enter data, continue, Microsoft login/passkey, callback, internal JWT stored, app/profile reachable.

## 10. Implementation Handoff Prompt
Implement this SDD spec exactly. Do not redesign architecture.

User goal:
RBJ-115 Feature: Passkey login. Invited users enter name/phone, authenticate with Microsoft Entra/passkey, backend atomically enrolls user and returns Workslip JWT.

Spec:
`/c/Workslip-worktrees/workslip-new-feature-20260612-154404/.hermes/specs/2026-06-12_1544-rbj-115-passkey-login.md`

Hard rules:
- Only change files listed in File-Level Change Plan unless compile/test failure proves another file is required.
- Preserve existing API output unless spec explicitly changes it.
- Write/update failing tests first where listed.
- Add Application transaction abstraction; do not inject `SqlDbContext` into Application service directly.
- Extend `CreateEntraUserResult` with created/existing signal before deleting on rollback; never delete a pre-existing Entra user.
- Frontend must not put Entra token in `AUTH_TOKEN_KEY`.
- If Azure/OIDC env variable names are missing in repo, use `VITE_AZURE_AD_TENANT_ID`, `VITE_AZURE_AD_CLIENT_ID`, `VITE_AZURE_AD_SCOPE`, `VITE_AZURE_AD_REDIRECT_URI` with clear runtime error when absent.
- Run exact verification commands.
- If an architectural decision is missing, stop and report the gap instead of inventing one.

Deliverables:
