# RBJ-104 FE UI Rework Implementation Plan

> For Hermes: planning only. Do not implement until user explicitly approves. Do not commit or push. Prompt before creating/switching branch.

Goal: Improve the Workslip mobile job-flow UI so it is easier to scan, easier to tap, and visually calmer without changing core functionality or backend contracts.

Architecture: Treat RBJ-104 as a frontend-only visual/hierarchy pass centered on the job step UI, especially `Arbejdssedler` / timesheets. Keep current components and data flow. Prefer CSS and small markup/class changes over new abstractions.

Tech stack: Vite React 19, TypeScript, React Router, lucide-react, existing Workslip CSS in `src/App.css` and global button tokens in `src/index.css`.

---

## Current context

Linear source: `RBJ-104 FE: UI Rework`.

Status: Backlog.

Observed repo state during planning:
- Branch: `rbj-55-app-page-6-digital-attestering`.
- Worktree dirty: yes, from RBJ-55 changes.
- Important: do not start RBJ-104 implementation on top of dirty RBJ-55 work unless user explicitly wants that. Safer path: finish/park RBJ-55, pull main, ask user before creating RBJ-104 branch.

Primary target area from Linear:
- Mobile job step UI.
- Especially tabs/step indicators, saved timesheets, timesheet form, summary, labels, tap targets, contrast, border noise.

Current relevant files inspected:
- `src/features/jobs/components/steps/JobWorksheetsStep.tsx`
- `src/features/jobs/components/steps/JobStepNavigation.tsx`
- `src/layouts/AppLayout.tsx`
- `src/App.css`
- `src/index.css`
- `package.json`

Key existing UI facts:
- Step tabs live in `StepIndicators` in `JobStepNavigation.tsx` and CSS `.step-indicators`, `.step-dot` around `src/App.css:1091`.
- Timesheet section uses `WorksheetsSection`, `WorksheetList`, `WorksheetTotalsSection`, `WorksheetDraftForm` in `JobWorksheetsStep.tsx`.
